{"type":"text","timestamp":1790320643769,"sessionID":"ses_f28948ce5ffe4nLH4LR7jGfAPD","part":{"id":"prt_0d76d0eac001sbny9PF5Ed1fRa","messageID":"msg_0d76cf3bb00175FDIOefWCQGzH","sessionID":"ses_f28948ce5ffe4nLH4LR7jGfAPD","type":"text","text":"Only benign ALSA audio errors (no sound card in the container) — no scene or shader errors. The task is complete:\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **`scripts/triplanar_basic.gdshader`** — Full spatial triplanar shader exactly per spec:\n   - `vec4 vertex = INV_VIEW_MATRIX * vec4(VERTEX, 1.0)` (world-space position)\n   - `vec3 normal = normalize((INV_VIEW_MATRIX * vec4(NORMAL, 0.0)).xyz)`\n   - `adjusted_normal = abs(normal)` and `weights = adjusted_normal / (adjusted_normal.x + adjusted_normal.y + adjusted_normal.z)`\n   - `uv_x = vertex.zy`, `uv_y = vertex.xz`, `uv_z = vertex.xy`\n   - Single `uniform sampler2D texture_x` sampled with all three UVs, each multiplied by its weight, `ALBEDO = color_x + color_y + color_z`\n\n2. **`scenes/main.tscn`** — Node3D scene with:\n   - `MeshInstance3D` sphere using a `SphereMesh` with a `ShaderMaterial` assigned to the **mesh's material property**\n   - Material references the shader with `texture_x` set to `res://assets/sprites/Rock022_2K-PNG_Color.png`\n   - Added `Camera3D` and `DirectionalLight3D` for visibility\n\n3. **`project.godot`** — Set `run/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"`\n\nRendered frames were verified visually: the sphere displays the rock texture projected triplanarly across its surface.","time":{"start":1790320643756,"end":1790320643758},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_122f33baa4ab4a6487dce4080a9b93ff_msg"}}}}
